        defendant: [.direct("Were you drinking?", "\"Two beers at the cookout. I had them over a couple of hours, with food, and I felt fine to drive.\""), .direct("Why were you on a tractor?", "\"It was how I got home. The farm is only a few miles from the cookout, and I took the back roads.\""), .direct("What happened on the road?", "\"The tractor drifted. The steering is loose, the road was rough, and I did not see the cars until they swerved.\""), .direct("Why did you refuse the breath test?", "\"I was scared. I did not understand what it would mean, and I did not want to make things worse.\""), .direct("Why did you sway on the walking test?", "\"I am old. My balance is not what it used to be, and I wobble on flat ground some days.\""), .direct("What do you want the trooper to know?", "\"I am sorry the drivers were frightened. I would never drive to hurt anyone.\""), .cross("You had been at a cookout, hadn't you?", "\"Yes. I ate, talked, and had two beers. I was not drunk.\""), .cross("The trooper smelled alcohol on you, didn't the trooper?", "\"The trooper says so. I had two beers, so I am not surprised.\""), .cross("You refused a breath test, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was scared, and I do not think I understood.\""), .cross("Two drivers went into a ditch because of your tractor, didn't they?", "\"I know. I am so sorry. The road was rough, and the steering is loose.\""), .cross("You crossed the center line, didn't you?", "\"The tractor did. I did not mean to, and I was not paying close attention.\"")],
        openings: ("At dusk, two drivers swerved into a ditch to avoid a tractor crossing the center line. A trooper stopped {D}'s tractor a mile on, smelled alcohol, saw glassy eyes, watched {D} fail a walking test, and {D} refused a breath test.", "{D} had two beers at a cookout and drove a tractor with loose steering over a rough road. An older driver who wobbles and is frightened of a test is not drunk by default."),
