        role: "Complainant",
        exam: [.direct("What can you tell us about your relationship with {D}?", "\"We were together, and I moved out about two months before this. I ended it because I felt controlled and unhappy.\""), .direct("What alerted you to the tracker?", "\"My phone warned that an unknown tracker was moving with me. I saw the alert, and I did not know what it meant at first.\""), .direct("Where was the tracker?", "\"A mechanic found a small tracker taped inside the rear bumper. I took the car in after the alert and the mechanic found it.\""), .direct("Whose account was the tracker registered to?", "\"{D}'s account and phone. The records tie the tracker to {D.him}, and the location log shows {D.his} phone following my route.\""), .direct("What did you notice over the next weeks?", "\"{D.He} turned up where I was. I saw {D.him} at my gym and at my work, and I felt that I was being watched everywhere.\""), .direct("How did this affect you?", "\"I was afraid to leave my home. I changed my routes and times, and I told my friends and my employer in case something happened.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever speak to you?", "\"Sometimes. {D.He} said hello when we saw each other. I did not want to talk, and I never agreed to a conversation.\""), .cross("Was there a threat?", "\"Not in words. {D.He} never said anything threatening. But the pattern made me afraid.\""), .cross("Does the defendant go to your gym?", "\"{D.He} says so. I do not know if {D.he} used that gym before. I only know that I saw {D.him} there after I moved out.\""), .cross("Could the tag have been left in the car by mistake?", "\"{D.He} says so. I do not know, but the tracker was taped inside the bumper, which is not where a person leaves a lost item.\""), .cross("Did the log show the defendant following hours later?", "\"Yes. The location log shows {D.his} phone following hours later. I do not know how to explain that.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} tracked and followed {V}.", "A tag left behind by mistake."),
