        summary: "On {DATE}, {V}, 19, a pledge at a fraternity house, was made to run drinking stations for two hours. {V}'s blood alcohol later measured 0.36. {V} fell down a flight of stairs and lay on a couch for hours while members waited before calling 911. {D}, the pledge master, set the rules and kept the vodka. {DL} says {D.he} told everyone to stop and thought {V} was sleeping.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Autopsy", "Blood alcohol 0.36 and a head injury."), E(.digital, 3, "Group Chat", "Messages setting the drinking rules."), E(.statement, 3, "Members", "Two members say {D} ran the stations."), E(.digital, 2, "911 Call", "Placed three hours after the fall.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Told Them to Stop", "{DL} says {D.he} told the house to stop.")],
        role: "Fraternity member (cooperating)",
        exam: [.direct("Tell the jury about your time in the fraternity.", "\"I am a member of the fraternity. I was at the house that night, and I am cooperating with the investigation because of what happened.\""), .direct("What was {V} made to do?", "\"{V}, who was 19, was a pledge. {V} was made to run drinking stations for two hours, with vodka and other drinks provided by the house.\""), .direct("Who set the rules?", "\"{D}, the pledge master, set the rules in a group chat and kept the vodka. Two members say {D.he} ran the stations.\""), .direct("What happened to {V}?", "\"{V} fell down a flight of stairs and lay on a couch for hours. Members waited before calling 911.\""), .direct("When was 911 called?", "\"About three hours after the fall. I did not call. I should have, and I think about it every day.\""), .direct("What did the autopsy show?", "\"A blood alcohol of 0.36 and a head injury. {V} died, and I learned later that the injury and the alcohol together were fatal.\""), .cross("Did {D} call 911?", "\"No. {D.He} did not call at first. {D.He} told members to wait before calling, and we did.\""), .cross("Did anyone object?", "\"A few members did. I remember someone saying we should call, but we did not.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say anything about stopping the drinking?", "\"{D.He} says {D.he} told everyone to stop. I do not remember that clearly, and I am not sure when it was said.\""), .cross("Did the defendant think {V} was sleeping?", "\"{DL} says so. {V} was on a couch, and many of us thought {V} had passed out. We did not check enough.\""), .cross("Why are you cooperating?", "\"I want to tell the truth. I feel responsible for what happened, and I want {V}'s family to know.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} forced a pledge to drink and waited to call for help.", "A pledge master who thought {V} was asleep."),
        allocution: "\"I should have walked away.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} wrote the drinking rules in a group chat.", "{DL} told members to wait before calling."),
        defendant: [.direct("What can you tell us about your role as pledge master?", "\"I helped run the pledge process. I wrote rules for the drinking stations, and I kept the vodka. I thought it was a tradition.\""), .direct("Did you set the rules?", "\"I helped. I wrote the rules in a group chat. I know now that those rules were dangerous, and I should not have written them.\""), .direct("What did you tell members when {V} fell?", "\"I told them to wait before calling. I thought {V} was sleeping. I did not realize {V} was seriously hurt.\""), .direct("Why did you wait to call 911?", "\"I thought {V} was just asleep. I was scared of getting the house in trouble. I know that is not an excuse.\""), .direct("Did you tell the house to stop the drinking?", "\"I told everyone to stop at some point. It was late, and I do not think anyone listened. I did not enforce it.\""), .direct("How do you feel about what happened?", "\"Horrible, more than anything. {V} died, and I did not call for help. I will carry that for the rest of my life.\""), .cross("The blood alcohol was 0.36, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I did not know it was that high. I should have realized, and I did not.\""), .cross("You wrote the rules in a group chat, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I called it a joke. I know it was not a joke, and I regret it a lot.\""), .cross("You told members to wait before calling, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I was wrong. I thought {V} was sleeping, and I did not check.\""), .cross("You kept the vodka, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I was in charge of it, and I know that makes me responsible.\""), .cross("Three hours passed before 911 was called, didn't they?", "\"Yes. That is what the call shows. I wish I could take back those hours.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, {V}, 19, a pledge at a fraternity house, was made to run drinking stations for two hours, and {V}'s blood alcohol later measured 0.36. {V} fell down a flight of stairs and lay on a couch for hours while members waited before calling 911.", "The defense will present a pledge master who thought {V} was sleeping, who told the house to stop, and who made a bad misjudgment. The State must prove what {D} knew and intended."),
        closings: ("A group chat that set the drinking rules, a pledge made to run stations, a blood alcohol of 0.36, and three hours before anyone called 911. {D} set the rules and kept the vodka.", "A bad misjudgment by a young person who thought {V} was only sleeping. The State must prove that {D} knew {V} was in danger and chose to wait."),
        timeline: [(-7, "The group chat rules."), (0, "The drinking stations."), (0, "Hours on the couch."), (0, "The 911 call.")],
        identified: "A group chat and an autopsy.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .male])

    static let stolenValorV1 = SmallCases.make(
