        defendant: [.direct("Describe your charity for the jury.", "\"I started a charity to build housing and memorials for veterans. It did real work, and it raised $340,000 over six years.\""), .direct("Did you serve in the military?", "\"No. I did not. I never served. I know that is the problem, and I am ashamed of it.\""), .direct("Why did you wear medals and a uniform?", "\"To raise money. I thought people would give more if I looked the part. I told stories for effect, and I know it was a lie.\""), .direct("Where did the medals come from?", "\"I bought them online. I did not earn them. I wore them at events, and I let people believe they were real.\""), .direct("What about the $90,000 paid to you?", "\"It was a salary for my work running the charity. I took it from the donations, and I did not disclose it clearly.\""), .direct("What would you say to {V}?", "\"I am so sorry. I used a lie to raise money, and I hurt people who trusted me. I wish I had told the truth from the start.\""), .cross("You never served, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I know it was wrong to tell a battle story as if I had.\""), .cross("You told a battle story at events, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I told it for effect. I know how it sounds, and I understand why people felt deceived.\""), .cross("You paid yourself $90,000, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I called it a salary. I know it was a large share of what was raised, and I did not tell donors.\""), .cross("You bought the medals online, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I wore them to look like a veteran, and I am not proud of it.\""), .cross("Donors gave because of your claims of service, didn't they?", "\"Some did. I know that. I did not stop them from believing it, and That is on me.\"")],
        openings: ("For six years, {D} spoke at Veterans Day events in a uniform with medals, telling of a battle overseas, and the charity raised $340,000. A reporter found that {D} never served, and $90,000 of the donations were paid to {D}.", "The defense will present a charity that did real work, housing that was built, and a speaker who did not claim a rank. {D} will not deny the lie about service, but will ask the jury to look at the whole story."),
