        threshold: 10,
        spec: "Unlawfully caused the death of {V}, age 17, by culpable negligence in operating a propane-fired liquor still in a barn, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 45...62,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, an explosion blew the roof off a barn on {D}'s property and started a fire that spread to a neighbor's barn. Inside was a large copper still fired by propane, and {V}, 17, a neighbor's child {D} paid $50 a night to watch the fire, died. The fire marshal found a loose propane fitting and no safety shutoff. {DL} says {V} changed the tank without being asked.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Fire Marshal Report", "A loose propane fitting and no shutoff."), E(.physical, 3, "Still", "A large still run on propane."), E(.statement, 3, "Neighbor", "{D} paid {V} $50 a night."), E(.forensic, 2, "Autopsy", "{V} died of smoke and burns.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Tank Swap", "{DL} says {V} swapped the tank without being told.")],
        role: "State fire marshal investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What do you do as a fire marshal investigator?", "\"I investigate explosions and fires for the state fire marshal. I examine origin and cause, interview witnesses, and inspect equipment for safety violations.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"An explosion blew the roof off a barn on {D}'s property and started a fire that spread to a neighbor's barn.\""), .direct("What did you find inside the barn?", "\"A large copper still fired by propane. The still ran on propane and had a loose fitting, and it had no safety shutoff.\""), .direct("What caused the blast?", "\"A loose propane fitting. Gas leaked and ignited. A shutoff would have stopped the flow, and there was none.\""), .direct("Who was inside at the time?", "\"{V}, who was 17, a neighbor's child that {DL} paid $50 a night to watch the fire. {V} died of smoke and burns.\""), .direct("What did you learn about safety training?", "\"{DL} paid {V} cash and never gave {V} any safety training. {DL} also installed the fitting {DL} did not check.\""), .cross("Who changed the tank?", "\"It is unclear. {D.He} says {V} swapped the tank without being told. I cannot say who handled it.\""), .cross("Was there a shutoff on the still?", "\"None. A shutoff would have helped, and its absence is a safety violation.\""), .cross("Did {V} know how the still worked?", "\"{V} was paid to watch the fire. I do not know how much {V} understood, and I do not know whether {V} was warned.\""), .cross("Who installed the loose fitting?", "\"{D.He} did. {D.He} installed the fitting, and I saw no sign of professional work.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell {V} to change the tank?", "\"{DL} says no. I cannot confirm that. The record shows {V} was paid to tend the fire.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used a teen to tend a dangerous still.", "A teen who changed the tank on {V.his} own."),
        allocution: "\"I let things get out of hand.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} paid {V} cash and never gave safety training.", "{DL} installed the fitting {D.himself}."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please describe your still.", "\"I built a copper still in my barn. I made moonshine, and I used propane to fire it. I know it is illegal, and I knew the risks.\""), .direct("Why did you hire {V}?", "\"{V} was a neighbor's child who wanted work. I paid $50 a night to watch the fire while I was away.\""), .direct("Did you tell {V} to change the tank?", "\"No. I did not. I told {V} to watch the fire. I did not tell {V} to touch the tank.\""), .direct("Did you train {V}?", "\"No. I did not give any safety training. I should have, and I know that was a failure.\""), .direct("Who installed the propane fitting?", "\"I did. I installed it myself. I should have hired someone, and I did not tighten it as I own that.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about what happened?", "\"If I am honest, I feel horrible. {V} died, and I will never forgive myself. I wish I had never built the still.\""), .cross("You paid {V} $50 a night, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I paid cash. I know I should not have hired a 17-year-old for that work.\""), .cross("There was no shutoff on the still, was there?", "\"No. I did not install one. I know it is a safety device, and That is on me.\""), .cross("You installed the fitting yourself, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I did not check it carefully, and I know it was loose.\""), .cross("You never gave {V} safety training, did you?", "\"No. I never did. I assumed {V} would be careful, and I was wrong.\""), .cross("{V} changed the tank without being asked, didn't {V}?", "\"I believe so. I did not tell {V} to. I know I am still responsible for the barn and the still.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, an explosion blew the roof off a barn on {D}'s property and started a fire that spread to a neighbor's barn. Inside was a large copper still fired by propane, and {V}, 17, whom {D} paid $50 a night to watch the fire, died.", "The defense will present a teenager who changed the tank on {V}'s own, a loose fitting, and a still that {D} did not hide. {D} admits the still, and asks the jury to look at who made the last decision."),
        closings: ("A loose propane fitting, no shutoff, a still run on propane, and a teenager paid $50 a night with no safety training. {V} died of smoke and burns in {D}'s barn.", "A teenager who swapped the tank on {V}'s own decision. The State must prove that {D}'s choices, not {V}'s, caused the explosion."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The still is built."), (-7, "{V} starts watching it."), (0, "The explosion."), (1, "The fire marshal arrives.")],
        identified: "A fire marshal's report.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .male])

    static let pharmacyRobberyV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.pharmacyRobbery",
        category: .robbery,
